<<~ ahu slot=`#/sources`>>

!! Sources
* Automerge Repo API, SharePolicy / ShareConfig / RepoConfig (search-only): https://automerge.org/automerge-repo/types/_automerge_react..ShareConfig.html , https://automerge.org/automerge-repo/types/_automerge_automerge_repo.SharePolicy.html . Snippets: sharePolicy runs when a doc is created/discovered (e.g. a peer starts syncing); shareConfig = `access` then `announce` (announce only after access); DEFAULT is announce-to-all and allow-all; marked experimental. NOT confirmed: behaviour for a peer connecting while an async policy input is unready.
* Saltzer and Schroeder 1975 "fail-safe defaults" (search-only): https://comp97109.doc.ic.ac.uk/reading/look-at-1975.pdf , https://shostack.org/blog/the-security-principles-of-saltzer-and-schroeder ; SoK on safe defaults https://arxiv.org/html/2412.17329v2 (generalises to defaults beyond access control; Massacci critique: deny is not always safe in cyber-physical systems).
* OWASP 2025 A10 "Mishandling of Exceptional Conditions" fail-closed vs fail-open (search-only, SECONDARY mirror, check owasp.org before citing): https://yisus-offsec.gitbook.io/offensive-and-defensive-security/documentation/offensive-security/publish-your-docs/owasp-top-10-2025/a10-2025-mishandling-of-exceptional-conditions ; CWE-636 summary https://shoulder.dev/threats/cwe/CWE-636 .
* Order-pin precedent: MIT krb5 plugorder.c (search-only) https://socsvn.freebsd.org/socsvn/mirror/FreeBSD/vendor-crypto/krb5/dist/src/tests/plugorder.c : registers modules, prints the order load_all returns, test diffs it. Also an IntelliJ forum thread noting a declared dependency may enforce availability, not init order (search-only). Search found no named JS-composer convention; weak evidence.
* Dead-code tooling: Knip (search-only; results were forks, check webpro-nl docs): exempt entry files, <code>&#64;public</code> JSDoc tag, `entry` array; advises specific exemptions over broad `ignore`. https://github.com/webpro/knip/blob/9f924ce4be4bf44fb6607150ced4d49a1a49c71f/docs/handling-issues.md

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/weighed-against-house-law`>>

!! Weighed against house law
* Fail-closed: precedent agrees with T11's lean (null cell = withhold). Automerge's own default is allow-all, so the house guard is the sole deny layer; a Repo-level default offers no backstop. Nothing found on pre-ready peers, so the "no peer before the cells stand" argument must be pinned by OUR test (N1), not borrowed. Massacci's caveat does not bite: deny here only withholds a doc, never a safety action.
* Order pin: krb5 pattern (record the order, assert it) fits; house-law fit good (red-first, no global: record via an injected list, no process global). Weak outside evidence, so this rests on house law.
* Unborn vs dead: the tooling answer is an explicit, named exemption (Knip <code>&#64;public</code>/entry), never silent. Maps to house law: an unborn seat carries its owed road row in the comment (the cure already ruled); a seat with no row and no canon is dead and burns. Conflict: tools key on reachability, the house keys on canon; the house rule wins, and a witness test could grep that each unborn seat names its row.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/floor-on-a-stale-store-smallest-red`>>

!! Floor-on-a-stale-store: smallest red
Claim to prove/refute: floor (sovereign null, custodyGroup null -> canon {} -> empty protected ids) on a storageDir holding a Kahu canon doc, a dialed peer asks for that doc id.
* Smallest (no boot): ShareInputs table through selfSlotShareDecision with protectedDocs ids = EMPTY (what the floor yields), hasWsSocket true / peerClass of a dial peer (weakest dialRelation), documentId = the Kahu canon id, selfSlotFedGate as the floor holds it. Assert false. REFUTES the leak if false (shelf/DenyAll closes it); PROVES it if true. Control: same peer asks a shelf-public doc, expect true; and the same Kahu ask with ids = {that id} expects false via the guard, to show the table moves.
* Boot form (confirmation only): floor boot on a scratch LAR_ROOT store pre-seeded with the canon doc + a stub dial peer; assert the doc never syncs out. Not run (read-only fence). Open input I did not read: what fedGate the floor hands the shelf for that doc id.

<<~/ahu>>

